1
00:00:15,310 --> 00:00:20,150
Unknown are the names
of the flowers that have been trampled

2
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:25,610
Birds have fallen to the earth
and long for the wind

3
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:30,700
Prayers won't solve anything

4
00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:36,040
Only the will to fight
can change the here and now!

5
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:41,340
O pigs who laugh at the resolve
to walk over corpses to move forward

6
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:43,880
Livestock complacency? False prosperity?

7
00:00:44,090 --> 00:00:46,760
Give us the freedom of dying,
starving wolves!

8
00:00:46,970 --> 00:00:52,140
The humiliation of being caged
is what triggers us to fight back

9
00:00:52,350 --> 00:00:57,440
We hunters slaughter prey
beyond the castle walls,

10
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:02,650
consumed with surging bloodlust,

11
00:01:02,860 --> 00:01:09,780
as our crimson bows and arrows
pierce scarlet holes into the twilight

12
00:01:31,988 --> 00:01:36,993
A Dim Light Amid Despair: Humanity's Comeback, Part 1

13
00:01:38,850 --> 00:01:39,810
Hey, you!

14
00:01:40,020 --> 00:01:40,900
Sir!

15
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:42,520
Who the hell are you?!

16
00:01:42,730 --> 00:01:45,690
Armin Arlelt, from Shiganshina District!

17
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:48,940
I see! That's a ridiculous name!
Did your parents give it to you?!

18
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:50,860
My grandfather did, Sir!

19
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:53,700
Arlelt! Why are you here?!

20
00:01:53,910 --> 00:01:55,740
To help humanity achieve victory!

21
00:01:55,950 --> 00:01:59,910
That's wonderful to hear!
We can feed you to the Titans!

22
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,040
Third row, about face!

23
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:04,540
Who the hell are you?!

24
00:02:04,750 --> 00:02:07,510
Sir! Thomas Wagner, from Trost District!

25
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:08,840
I can't hear you!

26
00:02:09,050 --> 00:02:10,420
- Thomas Wagner...
- Can't hear you!

27
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:12,430
- Look at them go.
- Go practice in a barn!

28
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:15,510
You went through the same thing
when you started as a cadet, didn't you?

29
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:16,970
It takes me back.

30
00:02:17,180 --> 00:02:20,230
No! You're from a pigsty!
You're less than livestock!

31
00:02:20,430 --> 00:02:22,440
Yes, Sir! I am less than livestock!

32
00:02:22,650 --> 00:02:24,480
- No!
- But what's all that intimidation for?

33
00:02:24,690 --> 00:02:26,110
It's a rite of passage.

34
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:28,400
We revert them to a blank slate
through the use of self-denial,

35
00:02:28,610 --> 00:02:32,110
after which we mold them into proper soldiers.

36
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:34,990
- Change it at once! Why are you here?!
- This is one step in that process.

37
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,280
To devote myself to humankind!

38
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:39,450
Fourth row, about face!

39
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:43,670
There are some he's not talking to...

40
00:02:43,870 --> 00:02:47,630
It's unnecessary for those who've
already been through their rites of passage.

41
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:51,720
They most likely witnessed the hell
that took place two years ago.

42
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:53,970
They have a different look on their faces.

43
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:56,510
Okay. Let's go.

44
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:57,890
Who the hell are you?!

45
00:02:58,100 --> 00:03:00,180
Jean Kirschtein, from Trost District!

46
00:03:00,390 --> 00:03:02,940
Why are you here?!

47
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:06,360
To join the Military Police Regiment
and live in the interior!

48
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:11,400
Oh. You wanna live in the interior, do you?

49
00:03:11,610 --> 00:03:13,110
Yes!

50
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:16,120
Who said you could sit?!

51
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:21,120
If you can't handle this,
you can forget about the Military Police!

52
00:03:21,330 --> 00:03:23,710
Who the hell are you?! Why are you here?!

53
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:27,040
Marco Bodt of Jinae, on the south side of Wall Rose!

54
00:03:27,250 --> 00:03:31,300
I want to join the Military Police Regiment
and give life and limb to the king!

55
00:03:31,510 --> 00:03:33,090
I see.

56
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:36,970
That's a fine goal, indeed. Go ahead and strive for it.

57
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:39,850
But, just so you know...

58
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:43,810
The king doesn't want your lousy life or limbs.

59
00:03:45,230 --> 00:03:48,310
You're next! Who the hell are you?!

60
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,400
Conny Springer!

61
00:03:49,610 --> 00:03:52,690
I'm from Ragako Village
on the south side of Wall Rose!

62
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:55,610
You have it backwards, Conny Springer!

63
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:57,620
It was the first thing you were taught!

64
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:02,700
This salute expresses your resolve
to give your heart to the people!

65
00:04:02,910 --> 00:04:07,000
Is your heart on your right side?!

66
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:17,300
Hey, you.

67
00:04:17,510 --> 00:04:19,430
What do you think you're doing?

68
00:04:23,470 --> 00:04:27,140
I'm talking to you! Who the hell are you?!

69
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:33,940
Sasha Braus from Dauper Village,
on the south side of Wall Rose!

70
00:04:34,150 --> 00:04:36,110
Sasha Braus...

71
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:39,280
What is that you're holding in your right hand?

72
00:04:39,490 --> 00:04:40,990
A steamed potato, Sir!

73
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:44,700
I found one in the cookhouse
that was ready to eat, so I couldn't help myself!

74
00:04:44,910 --> 00:04:47,080
You stole it?

75
00:04:47,290 --> 00:04:48,500
Why?

76
00:04:48,710 --> 00:04:51,170
Why did you decide to eat it now?

77
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:54,380
I felt it would be a waste to let it get cold,

78
00:04:54,590 --> 00:04:57,420
so I elected to eat it now.

79
00:04:57,630 --> 00:05:00,390
No, I don't understand.

80
00:05:00,590 --> 00:05:03,350
Why did you eat the potato?

81
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:09,730
Are you asking me why people eat potatoes, Sir?

82
00:05:23,490 --> 00:05:26,910
Here's half of it for you.

83
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,960
Half...?

84
00:05:33,790 --> 00:05:37,380
Whoa. He still has Potato Girl running.

85
00:05:37,590 --> 00:05:40,630
Man, she's been at it for five solid hours.
She's really something.

86
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:44,220
Still, being told to run
until she's on the verge of death

87
00:05:44,430 --> 00:05:48,770
didn't seem to bother her quite as much
as being told she has to skip meals.

88
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:55,020
Dauper's a small hunting village
in the mountains, isn't it?

89
00:05:55,230 --> 00:05:56,320
What's that?

90
00:05:56,530 --> 00:06:00,400
They're dropouts. They asked
to work in the fields instead.

91
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:03,530
Whoa. It's only the first day, too...

92
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:07,450
That's just how it is. If you
can't cut it here, you have to leave.

93
00:06:09,460 --> 00:06:13,750
I can't believe anyone would want
to pick up rocks and pull plants again...

94
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:17,670
Come to think of it, we haven't heard
anything about where you're from.

95
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:21,010
I'm from Shiganshina, same as him.

96
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:23,300
Oh. That means...

97
00:06:23,510 --> 00:06:25,300
You were there that day, weren't you?

98
00:06:25,510 --> 00:06:26,510
H-Hey!

99
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:29,310
Did you see the Colossal Titan?!

100
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:31,600
Y-Yeah...

101
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:37,860
Yes, I saw it.

102
00:06:38,070 --> 00:06:39,070
Really?!

103
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:40,990
How big is it?!

104
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:43,030
Enough to look over the wall.

105
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:45,950
What?! I heard it stepped over the wall!

106
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:46,950
Me too!

107
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:48,790
That's what they said in my village too!

108
00:06:48,990 --> 00:06:51,660
No, it wasn't that big.

109
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:53,710
What did it look like?!

110
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:57,710
It had a huge mouth, and almost no skin.

111
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:00,670
What about the Armored Titan
that broke Wall Maria?!

112
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:05,220
That's what people call it, but it
looked like an ordinary Titan to me.

113
00:07:05,430 --> 00:07:08,220
Th-Then, what are ordinary Titans like?!

114
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:19,690
Let's spare him the questions, everyone.

115
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:22,030
I'm sure there are things
he doesn't want to remember.

116
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,200
Sorry for asking...

117
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:25,280
It's not like that!

118
00:07:29,030 --> 00:07:32,250
Titans aren't actually that big of a deal!

119
00:07:32,450 --> 00:07:36,500
Once we've mastered omni-directional mobility gear,

120
00:07:36,710 --> 00:07:38,540
they'll be nothing to us!

121
00:07:38,750 --> 00:07:41,550
We finally get to train as soldiers.

122
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:44,510
I was just overcome with emotion, that's all.

123
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:48,760
I'm going to join the Scout Regiment
and drive the Titans out of this world!

124
00:07:48,970 --> 00:07:50,220
I'm gonna slaughter them!

125
00:07:50,430 --> 00:07:52,770
Whoa, what are you, crazy?

126
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:56,770
Did you just say you're gonna join
the Scout Regiment?

127
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:59,110
Yeah, that's right.

128
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:01,780
Aren't you the one
who wants to join the Military Police

129
00:08:01,980 --> 00:08:03,690
and live the easy life?

130
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:06,110
I'm all about being honest, you see.

131
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:09,740
It's much nicer than being,
say, a loser who acts tough

132
00:08:09,950 --> 00:08:12,410
but is actually scared shitless.

133
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:14,870
Are you talking about me?!

134
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:16,830
S-Stop...!

135
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,170
Come on, now.

136
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:20,090
It makes no difference to me.

137
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:31,680
Look, I'm sorry.

138
00:08:31,890 --> 00:08:35,140
I don't mean to dismiss your ideas.

139
00:08:35,350 --> 00:08:37,270
Let's be friends.

140
00:08:38,650 --> 00:08:41,060
Yeah, I'm sorry, too.

141
00:08:55,830 --> 00:08:57,660
H-Hey, you!

142
00:08:58,750 --> 00:09:02,670
Uhh, err, umm...

143
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:06,090
I've just never seen anyone
who looks like you before...

144
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:08,380
S-Sorry!

145
00:09:08,590 --> 00:09:11,050
You have very pretty black hair.

146
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:12,720
Thanks.

147
00:09:21,690 --> 00:09:23,730
It's no big deal. Get off my back.

148
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:26,690
You never think things through
when you get worked up.

149
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,610
That again?

150
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:32,490
Anyway, don't you think your hair's too long?

151
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:36,120
It could cause an accident
during ODM training, you know.

152
00:09:36,330 --> 00:09:39,080
All right. I'll cut it.

153
00:09:39,290 --> 00:09:42,250
But how short should I make it?

154
00:09:46,550 --> 00:09:49,470
H-Hey! Don't mess with other people's clothes!

155
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:51,470
What did you wipe on me?!

156
00:09:53,140 --> 00:09:56,600
My trust in others...

157
00:09:59,430 --> 00:10:02,100
Finally... done...

158
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:23,960
This is...!

159
00:10:24,170 --> 00:10:24,790
Bread!

160
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:29,050
It's not much, but I saved it for you.

161
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:30,760
Oh, but...

162
00:10:30,970 --> 00:10:33,220
You really ought to drink some water first.

163
00:10:37,010 --> 00:10:37,930
- Are you God?!
- Huh?!

164
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:39,310
- Are you?!
- Uhh...!

165
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:40,600
God!

166
00:10:40,810 --> 00:10:44,900
Hey. What are you two doing?

167
00:10:45,110 --> 00:10:49,440
Umm, she's been running
non-stop all this time, so...

168
00:10:49,650 --> 00:10:52,740
So you're trying to do something "nice," huh?

169
00:10:52,950 --> 00:10:54,240
Huh?!

170
00:10:59,410 --> 00:11:02,120
Did you do it for Potato Girl's sake?

171
00:11:02,330 --> 00:11:05,830
Was what you gained worth the effort it took?

172
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:11,630
Well, whatever.

173
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:14,890
Let's just get her to her bed now.

174
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:18,810
Are you trying to be nice, too?

175
00:11:19,010 --> 00:11:22,180
I'm doing this so that she'll owe me.

176
00:11:22,390 --> 00:11:24,980
Her stupidity will come in very handy.

177
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:31,780
We'll begin by determining your aptitude!

178
00:11:31,990 --> 00:11:35,070
If you can't do this, you're not even fit to be bait!

179
00:11:35,280 --> 00:11:37,320
You'll be sent off to the fields!

180
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:41,080
These are only just the bare fundamentals.

181
00:11:41,290 --> 00:11:44,540
Still, you can determine a person's knack
for omni-mobility at this stage.

182
00:11:45,830 --> 00:11:47,250
Observe.

183
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:49,500
Completely steady.

184
00:11:49,710 --> 00:11:53,300
She knows exactly what to do and how to do it.

185
00:11:53,510 --> 00:11:56,590
That's what aptitude is all about.

186
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:59,510
It looks like we have many talented cadets this year.

187
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:02,310
Umm, what about him?

188
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:05,350
Now that's the very definition of aptitude.

189
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:07,690
Some people might have plenty of motivation...

190
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:10,900
...yet turn out to be less-than-capable.

191
00:12:11,110 --> 00:12:12,860
What are you doing, Eren Jaeger?!

192
00:12:13,070 --> 00:12:14,860
Straighten yourself up!

193
00:12:16,030 --> 00:12:17,410
What the...?!

194
00:12:17,610 --> 00:12:20,280
How do I work this thing?!

195
00:12:20,490 --> 00:12:22,040
This can't be for real...

196
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:37,430
Just follow the basics and you'll be able to do it.

197
00:12:37,630 --> 00:12:39,930
Don't think about being fancy or anything.

198
00:12:40,140 --> 00:12:42,390
Focus on your front and back balance,

199
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:46,020
then slowly place your weight
into the belts on your waist and feet.

200
00:12:46,230 --> 00:12:50,060
You can do it if you stay calm.
Even I did it, after all.

201
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:52,980
All right. I feel like I've got it this time.

202
00:12:53,190 --> 00:12:54,990
Lift me up, Armin.

203
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:11,250
Hey, Daz.

204
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:16,300
Isn't he the one who said he was
gonna slaughter all the Titans yesterday?

205
00:13:16,510 --> 00:13:19,340
I guess it's off to the fields for him tomorrow.

206
00:13:19,550 --> 00:13:21,930
Yeah, we can't afford to feed the useless.

207
00:13:22,140 --> 00:13:24,430
Eren!

208
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:26,680
There's no point worrying about it.

209
00:13:26,890 --> 00:13:29,520
You can just learn to do it tomorrow.

210
00:13:29,730 --> 00:13:31,440
I'm pathetic...

211
00:13:31,650 --> 00:13:35,070
There's no way I can wipe them out like this...

212
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:38,200
You should just forget about that altogether.

213
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:39,860
What?!

214
00:13:40,070 --> 00:13:42,950
I'm saying you should give up trying to be a soldier.

215
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:46,870
Fighting isn't about simply throwing your life away.

216
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:51,170
Hey, now! I saw what happened that day!

217
00:13:51,370 --> 00:13:54,170
Do you really think
you can just convince me to quit?!

218
00:13:54,380 --> 00:13:57,170
Still, it doesn't matter how determined you are.

219
00:13:57,380 --> 00:13:59,670
Huh? Why not?!

220
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:04,180
Because you don't get to decide
if you're fit to be a soldier or not.

221
00:14:10,980 --> 00:14:13,610
- I'm not saying you should return...
- Let's go, Armin.

222
00:14:13,810 --> 00:14:15,770
- ...to the fields by yourself.
- Y-Yeah.

223
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:17,940
You don't need to worry.

224
00:14:18,150 --> 00:14:22,160
Because when you go, I'll go with you.

225
00:14:26,370 --> 00:14:29,540
So, umm... What you're saying is...

226
00:14:29,750 --> 00:14:32,960
...that I can have that?

227
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:53,400
The trick to posture control?

228
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:57,400
Sorry, but I'm gifted. All I can tell you is to "feel" it.

229
00:14:57,610 --> 00:14:59,650
If anything, I'd like to hear your trick

230
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:04,860
for staying sane after
putting on such a pathetic spectacle.

231
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:08,620
C'mon, guys! I'm begging you here!

232
00:15:08,830 --> 00:15:14,620
But didn't you say yesterday,
"If you can't cut it here, you have to leave"?

233
00:15:14,830 --> 00:15:19,250
Or, wait. Was it, "If you don't got talent,
you have to leave"?

234
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:21,130
Which was it again?

235
00:15:21,340 --> 00:15:25,090
Please! I heard you're both really good at it!

236
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:27,100
Bertholdt! Reiner!

237
00:15:27,890 --> 00:15:31,730
Sorry, but I don't think there are
any tricks to just hanging there.

238
00:15:31,930 --> 00:15:35,150
I can't think of any especially helpful advice, either.

239
00:15:35,350 --> 00:15:36,310
Oh...

240
00:15:36,520 --> 00:15:38,820
I guess we'll just have to hope for the best tomorrow.

241
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:44,200
You two are, umm, from Shiganshina, aren't you?

242
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:45,740
Yeah...

243
00:15:45,950 --> 00:15:48,950
Then you know how terrifying the Titans are.

244
00:15:49,160 --> 00:15:51,490
So why do you want to be soldiers?

245
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:59,880
Unlike Eren, I didn't witness
the Titan threat firsthand.

246
00:16:00,090 --> 00:16:01,130
It's just...

247
00:16:01,340 --> 00:16:04,260
I decided I couldn't sit there
and do nothing after the royal government

248
00:16:04,470 --> 00:16:08,090
forced people into
that absolutely awful retrieval operation.

249
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:09,640
Oh.

250
00:16:09,850 --> 00:16:12,310
Where are you two from?

251
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:14,930
Reiner and I are from a mountain village

252
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:17,350
on the southeast side of Wall Maria.

253
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:19,440
Huh?! Wasn't that...?

254
00:16:19,650 --> 00:16:20,730
Yeah.

255
00:16:20,940 --> 00:16:23,030
Unlike the prosperous towns along the river,

256
00:16:23,230 --> 00:16:25,700
we didn't receive word right away.

257
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:30,530
The Titans showed up
well before the information did.

258
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:32,990
It happened at dawn.

259
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:35,580
The livestock were acting up,

260
00:16:35,790 --> 00:16:39,880
and these strange rumblings
kept getting louder and louder.

261
00:16:40,090 --> 00:16:44,710
At some point, I realized
they were footfalls of some sort...

262
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:48,510
And then, when I hurriedly opened the window...

263
00:16:56,640 --> 00:17:01,820
After that... l, umm, don't really remember.

264
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:03,530
Everyone was in such a panic...

265
00:17:03,730 --> 00:17:07,240
Hey, now. What are you
suddenly bringin' that up for?

266
00:17:07,450 --> 00:17:08,780
Sorry.

267
00:17:08,990 --> 00:17:11,700
Basically, what I was trying to say

268
00:17:11,910 --> 00:17:15,790
is that you guys probably aren't like them.

269
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:16,870
"Them"?

270
00:17:17,080 --> 00:17:20,380
The others here who don't know
the horror of the Titans.

271
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:21,840
Hey!

272
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:33,930
They're mostly here for show;
to live up to society's expectations.

273
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:37,810
You're seen as a coward if you choose
production work when you turn twelve.

274
00:17:38,020 --> 00:17:40,810
Society has pushed them into becoming cadets.

275
00:17:42,150 --> 00:17:46,400
That said, I'm no different than them.

276
00:17:46,610 --> 00:17:48,900
I chose to be a soldier
in the hopes of joining the Military Police

277
00:17:49,110 --> 00:17:51,320
so I could work in safety of the interior.

278
00:17:51,530 --> 00:17:55,540
If that doesn't work out, I might give up entirely.

279
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:59,500
I don't have any will to call my own, you see.

280
00:17:59,710 --> 00:18:04,420
Cherishing your life is admirable too, you know.

281
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:08,720
As for me...

282
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:11,300
I'm going to return to the hometown we lost.

283
00:18:11,510 --> 00:18:13,760
That's all I care about now.

284
00:18:15,180 --> 00:18:18,220
I will do it, no matter what.

285
00:18:20,060 --> 00:18:22,310
What about you?

286
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:24,480
Why do you want to be a soldier?

287
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:27,980
I...

288
00:18:33,030 --> 00:18:36,120
I decided I have to kill them.

289
00:18:36,330 --> 00:18:40,040
I decided I have to slaughter all the Titans

290
00:18:40,250 --> 00:18:43,080
with my own two hands.

291
00:18:47,210 --> 00:18:51,420
So, your encounter with the Titans
didn't break your will?

292
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:52,510
That's right...

293
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:54,510
But now it's a question of whether or not

294
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:57,430
I'm actually cut out to be a soldier.

295
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:19,490
Start over from scratch,
starting with your belt adjustment.

296
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:22,370
You'll do just fine tomorrow.

297
00:19:22,580 --> 00:19:24,670
I'm certain of it.

298
00:19:24,870 --> 00:19:27,710
Eren Jaeger, was it?

299
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:30,340
Yeah. Thanks.

300
00:19:30,550 --> 00:19:33,090
Reiner Braun, right?

301
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:45,770
Eren Jaeger. Are you ready?

302
00:19:45,980 --> 00:19:46,980
Yes, Sir!

303
00:19:47,190 --> 00:19:50,150
I'm going to do it! I am!

304
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:53,190
I might not have raw aptitude,

305
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:56,780
but no one has more guts than I do!

306
00:19:56,990 --> 00:19:58,490
Begin!

307
00:20:05,870 --> 00:20:07,670
The hell with logic!

308
00:20:07,880 --> 00:20:09,540
I know it's completely baseless!

309
00:20:09,750 --> 00:20:12,800
But guts are all I got!

310
00:20:13,760 --> 00:20:14,670
They're...

311
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,800
...my weapon!

312
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:22,520
I did it!

313
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:24,310
I'm doing it!

314
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:35,150
N-Not yet!

315
00:20:35,360 --> 00:20:38,030
I can still do it!

316
00:20:39,490 --> 00:20:40,990
Let him down.

317
00:20:45,580 --> 00:20:48,420
I-I'm...!

318
00:20:49,290 --> 00:20:52,300
Wagner. Switch belts with Jaeger.

319
00:20:52,500 --> 00:20:53,920
Y-Yes, Sir!

320
00:21:01,850 --> 00:21:04,100
Your equipment was defective.

321
00:21:04,310 --> 00:21:08,350
The belt you were using had a broken clasp.

322
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:11,690
I've never heard of this part breaking before;

323
00:21:11,900 --> 00:21:14,900
I guess we'll have to add it
to the maintenance checklist.

324
00:21:15,110 --> 00:21:18,660
Then, even with broken equipment,
he still managed to...?!

325
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:20,370
Whoa!

326
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:24,120
Th-Then, am I fit to be a soldier?!

327
00:21:24,330 --> 00:21:27,500
You pass muster. Train hard!

328
00:21:28,460 --> 00:21:31,000
I did it! I did it!

329
00:21:31,210 --> 00:21:34,250
Whadya think of that, Mikasa?! I can do it!

330
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:36,760
I can fight the Titans!

331
00:21:36,970 --> 00:21:40,180
You can finally stop mollycoddling me!

332
00:21:41,510 --> 00:21:43,470
Looks like things worked out for him.

333
00:21:43,680 --> 00:21:45,850
His eyes say, "What do you think of that?!"

334
00:21:46,060 --> 00:21:47,230
No.

335
00:21:48,940 --> 00:21:53,820
He feels relieved that
he doesn't have to leave me now.

336
00:21:57,070 --> 00:21:58,400
Grisha...

337
00:21:58,610 --> 00:22:03,450
Today, your son has become a soldier.

338
00:22:39,530 --> 00:22:44,240
Your dreams are where your heart is

339
00:22:44,450 --> 00:22:50,500
They're more fragile than life itself

340
00:22:50,710 --> 00:22:55,210
Over and over you cast them aside,
only to find more

341
00:22:55,420 --> 00:23:01,920
Now, rest in peace

342
00:23:02,130 --> 00:23:13,020
Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for

343
00:23:13,230 --> 00:23:23,530
and the more we forget
the more we remember again

344
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:29,490
In this beautiful, cruel world

345
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:34,790
all I can do is ask why we're still alive

346
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:40,420
Oh, with our strength...and our weakness...

347
00:23:40,630 --> 00:23:45,970
what are we going to protect if there's no sense

348
00:23:46,180 --> 00:23:50,770
to anything anymore?

349
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:58,860
After graduating from the Cadets,

350
00:23:59,070 --> 00:24:02,780
Eren sees humanity and its regained dignity.

351
00:24:02,990 --> 00:24:04,610
"We can beat the Titans."

352
00:24:04,820 --> 00:24:07,759
The moment he feels certain of this,
humanity is reminded yet again...

353
00:24:07,759 --> 00:24:09,580
The Night of the Closing Ceremony: Humanity's Comeback, Part 2
The moment he feels certain of this,
humanity is reminded yet again...

354
00:24:09,580 --> 00:24:09,969
The Night of the Closing Ceremony: Humanity's Comeback, Part 2
